      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we did that, we might end up copying out more than \"the smallest (SHA1) digest\", as the comment says. I take it the comment is an assertion about some cr50 API/ABI invariant that we can\u0027t copy out more than 20 bytes, even in the case of SHA-256?\n\nIf we did\n\n```\nunsigned int length;\nEVP_DigestFinal(ctx, full_digest, \u0026length);\nmemcpy(block_digest, full_digest, MIN(size, length));\n```\n\nand if the hash function were SHA-256, and if `size` were `SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH`, we\u0027d have `MIN(32, 32)` which would seem to violate the invariant.\n\nOr, maybe that would be correct, and we should update the comment. I don\u0027t know the expectations that callers have.",
